From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas Villar <15879262+nvillar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:54:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Vanilla: AOSP WebView as the default provider, and add Jelly

The vanilla image had no active WebView provider. Android 16's
WebViewUpdateServiceImpl2 takes the provider the user chose, otherwise the
first availableByDefault entry of config_webview_packages and nothing after
it; treble-overlay-highpriomisc (vendor/hardware_overlay, static, priority
8998) lists Google WebView first, which vanilla does not ship. So every
WebView-using app failed ("No WebView installed") until
`cmd webviewupdate set-webview-implementation com.android.webview`.

generate.sh now makes the vanilla products inherit duo-vanilla.mk, which adds:
- DuoVanillaWebViewOverlay: static RRO on android, priority 9100, whose
  provider list is only com.android.webview (the preinstalled AOSP WebView
  package, the LineageOS Chromium prebuilt from the DUO-DE manifest);
- Jelly (LineageOS packages/apps/Jelly, Soong android_app, Apache-2.0),
  which overrides Browser2.

GApps products do not inherit duo-vanilla.mk and keep Google WebView first.
The user's choice in Developer options still wins while it is valid.

Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 duo-vanilla.mk                                     | 11 +++++++++++
 duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/Android.bp              |  7 +++++++
 duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/AndroidManifest.xml     | 10 ++++++++++
 .../res/xml/config_webview_packages.xml            | 14 ++++++++++++++
 generate.sh                                        |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 duo-vanilla.mk
 create mode 100644 duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/Android.bp
 create mode 100644 duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/AndroidManifest.xml
 create mode 100644 duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/res/xml/config_webview_packages.xml

diff --git a/duo-vanilla.mk b/duo-vanilla.mk
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1763f73
--- /dev/null
+++ b/duo-vanilla.mk
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# DUO-DE: additions for the vanilla (no GApps) variant only. generate.sh
+# inherits this file from the treble_*_?v? products; GApps products do not.
+
+# Google WebView is absent on vanilla: make the preinstalled AOSP WebView
+# (com.android.webview, the LineageOS Chromium prebuilt) the default provider.
+PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+    DuoVanillaWebViewOverlay
+
+# LineageOS Jelly, a basic browser on the system WebView (replaces Browser2).
+PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+    Jelly
diff --git a/duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/Android.bp b/duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/Android.bp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f08faf0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/Android.bp
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+// DUO-DE vanilla only (device/phh/treble/duo-vanilla.mk): WebView provider list
+// with the preinstalled AOSP WebView as the default provider.
+runtime_resource_overlay {
+    name: "DuoVanillaWebViewOverlay",
+    sdk_version: "current",
+    product_specific: true,
+}
diff --git a/duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/AndroidManifest.xml b/duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/AndroidManifest.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8909b3d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<!-- Above treble-overlay-highpriomisc (vendor/hardware_overlay, priority 8998),
+     which lists Google WebView first. -->
+<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
+    package="dev.duode.overlay.vanilla.webview">
+    <overlay
+        android:targetPackage="android"
+        android:priority="9100"
+        android:isStatic="true" />
+</manifest>
diff --git a/duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/res/xml/config_webview_packages.xml b/duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/res/xml/config_webview_packages.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d0c50b8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/duo-vanilla/WebViewOverlay/res/xml/config_webview_packages.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<!-- DUO-DE vanilla: WebView providers.
+
+     Android 16's WebViewUpdateServiceImpl2 uses the provider the user chose in
+     Developer options if it is valid, otherwise the FIRST availableByDefault
+     provider of this list, and never falls through to later entries. The
+     treble list (treble-overlay-highpriomisc) starts with Google WebView, which
+     vanilla does not ship, so a fresh vanilla install had no WebView at all.
+     Vanilla preinstalls only the AOSP WebView package (the LineageOS Chromium
+     prebuilt), so it is the only provider listed. -->
+<webviewproviders>
+    <webviewprovider description="Android System WebView" packageName="com.android.webview" availableByDefault="true">
+    </webviewprovider>
+</webviewproviders>
diff --git a/generate.sh b/generate.sh
index 50912a8..1272b0d 100644
--- a/generate.sh
+++ b/generate.sh
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ for part in a ab;do
 				fi
 				if [ "$apps" == "vanilla" ];then
 					apps_suffix="v"
-					apps_script=''
+					apps_script='$(call inherit-product, device/phh/treble/duo-vanilla.mk)'
 					apps_name="vanilla"
 				fi
 				if [ "$apps" == "old" ];then
